SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday? Beaver Dam 26R
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRIDE LEADER: Jan Zerfoss\
 , average pace 12-13 mph.\nCue and Ride with GPS link: [Beaver Dam](https:
 //ridewithgps.com/routes/48541205)\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride Togeth
 er**\n\nThis is a casual ride and the ride leader will ride at the adverti
 sed pace. Some riders may ride faster than the leader so we'll likely brea
 k into one or more smaller groups. We will stop to regroup periodically. P
 lease stay with other riders in your pace group so everyone has someone to
  ride with and nobody is riding solo. Usually no designated sweep but nobo
 dy will get dropped.\n\nIntercourse Park has well maintained restrooms tha
 t are usually open.\n\nPost-ride coffee/refreshments - BYO refreshments to
  enjoy in the shade of the park pavilion.\n\nHelmets are mandatory. No ear
 buds. Please bring water and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\
 , pump/CO2 inflator).\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and paper waive
 r\, we require LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride
 . Being on\nMeetup does not mean you are a club member. Join here [Member 
 Signup](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=
 257148)\n\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Cond
 uct: [Code of Conduct](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page
 _id=22&club_id=257148&module_id=323984)\n\nGuidance if an incident occurs:
  [Incident Actions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&
 club_id=257148&module_id=326137)
